{"id": "triple-6-all", "kind": "triple", "note": "Trunk allowing all VLANs: add is a no-op, replace pins it to an explicit list, remove is answered with a clarification in training (the compiler refuses the raw plan — that refusal is an engine test, not a training label).", "before": {"device": "sw-acc-1", "hostname": "switch1", "vlans": {"10": {"name": "Users"}, "20": {"name": "Engineering"}}, "interfaces": {"GigabitEthernet1/0/48": {"mode": "trunk", "access_vlan": 1, "trunk_allowed": "all", "native_vlan": 1, "admin": "up", "description": "Uplink to core", "aliases": ["uplink"]}}}, "cases": [{"verb": "add", "request": "Add VLAN 20 to the uplink trunk", "plan": {"device": "sw-acc-1", "operation": "add_trunk_vlans", "interface": "GigabitEthernet1/0/48", "vlans": [20]}, "after": {"device": "sw-acc-1", "hostname": "switch1", "vlans": {"10": {"name": "Users"}, "20": {"name": "Engineering"}}, "interfaces": {"GigabitEthernet1/0/48": {"mode": "trunk", "access_vlan": 1, "trunk_allowed": "all", "native_vlan": 1, "admin": "up", "description": "Uplink to core", "aliases": ["uplink"]}}}}, {"verb": "replace", "request": "Restrict the uplink trunk to only VLAN 20", "plan": {"device": "sw-acc-1", "operation": "replace_trunk_vlans", "interface": "GigabitEthernet1/0/48", "vlans": [20]}, "after": {"device": "sw-acc-1", "hostname": "switch1", "vlans": {"10": {"name": "Users"}, "20": {"name": "Engineering"}}, "interfaces": {"GigabitEthernet1/0/48": {"mode": "trunk", "access_vlan": 1, "trunk_allowed": [20], "native_vlan": 1, "admin": "up", "description": "Uplink to core", "aliases": ["uplink"]}}}}, {"verb": "remove", "request": "Remove VLAN 20 from the uplink trunk", "expected_clarify": {"type": "clarify", "reason": "unsupported_remove_from_all", "question": "GigabitEthernet1/0/48 allows all VLANs, and removing a single VLAN from 'all' is not supported. What should the trunk's allowed VLAN list be?", "candidates": []}, "expected_after_equals_before": true, "note": "Training label: clarify with reason unsupported_remove_from_all, zero state change. The raw remove_trunk_vlans plan for this state is refused by the compiler; that refusal stays covered as an ENGINE test (gold-remove-from-all-errors, scripts/test_entry_points.py), not as a training label."}]}
